cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "Drone Landing on a Moving Platform: a vision-based autonomous quadrotor recovery stack"
abstract: >-
  A research-grade simulation stack for autonomous quadrotor landing on moving
  platforms (ground rovers and 6-DOF seakeeping ship decks), flying on onboard
  sensors only (no ground truth in the loop). Includes ArUco perception with a
  relative-state Kalman filter, a landing-supervisor finite-state machine,
  geometric / nonlinear-MPC / image-based-visual-servoing control, residual
  reinforcement learning, formal safety (Hamilton-Jacobi reachability and
  control-barrier-function shields), maritime fidelity (wave spectra, RAOs, and
  ship air-wake), and a separate decentralized multi-drone swarm module.
type: software
authors:
